{"title":"1997 JBMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_JBMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/defbf06b987965438e5928b96688e48df84cba0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c5df946080fc6ec1ee0a560a8e8c5e6699113c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/3958e984d2597b35da7975f4503cdcf965a777f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ldots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/4/a74b5d37373c0f9f3c0b0f76d9d5decd42d4f13c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{1998}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> be positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/27994bc5861679d68c68e81da1b333f9770e3752.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n_1^2 + n_2^2 + \\cdots + n_{1997}^2 = n_{1998}^2.\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"19\" /> Show that at least two of the numbers are even.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_JBMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In order to prove that at least two numbers are even, we need to prove that it is impossible to have exactly one number even and that it is impossible to have exactly no numbers even.\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Lemma 1: Impossible to have exactly 1 number even</b><br />\nAssume one of the numbers is even.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/4/a74b5d37373c0f9f3c0b0f76d9d5decd42d4f13c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{1998}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> is even, then the left side is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> while the right side is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1d1407aac4125d6c453a365eb173d96ebb48e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> which can not happen.  If one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/d/ebdcdac82a1c504530367b6520e54bac158dcfc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1, n_2, \\cdots n_{1997}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"114\" height=\"11\" /> is even, then the left side is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> while the right side is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1d1407aac4125d6c453a365eb173d96ebb48e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> which can not happen.  Thus, it is impossible for exactly one of the numbers to be even.\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Lemma 2: Impossible to have all numbers odd</b><br />\nAssume all numbers are odd (or that there are no even numbers).  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/b/7eb75ccf06e046206cb4c636a54d7be11d049fbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is odd for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/1/ca139ebed4e477be7bf6ff902536360f274e985d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i \\le 1998,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/4/054d736f3f6e5f9a5f9a8469530573bdf7b5533c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_i^2 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{8}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"19\" />  That means the left side is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> while the right side is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/1/bb13a1ea7b9fd6892ebe9599c3587aa68288c873.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />  Since this can not happen, it is impossible for none of the numbers to be even.\n</p><p><br />\nSince it’s impossible to have exactly one or zero even numbers, at least two of the integers must be even.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_JBMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_JBMO\" title=\"1997 JBMO\">1997 JBMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_JBMO_Problems\" title=\"1997 JBMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13_contests\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_JBMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 JBMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1997 JBMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1997 JBMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1997 JBMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_JBMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 JBMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a><b></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JBMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" title=\"JBMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\"> All JBMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017190648\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.034 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 143/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 882/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 46/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3856/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.534      1 Template:JBMO_box\n100.00%    7.534      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15705:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017190648 and revision id 96850. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}